 "result": "**Mechanism:** werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects backed by a `ContextVar`.\n\n- `src/tessel/globals.py:40` defines a single `ContextVar`, `_app_var`. It holds the current `AppContext`.\n- `src/tessel/globals.py:41-62` builds each global as a `LocalProxy` over that variable. Each one resolves an attribute of the current `AppContext` on every access:\n  - `active_app` is `AppContext.app` (line 44)\n  - `g` is `AppContext.g` (line 47)\n  - `request` is `AppContext.request` (line 57)\n  - `session` is `AppContext.session` (line 60)\n  - `app_ctx` is the `AppContext` itself (line 41)\n- `src/tessel/ctx.py:433` binds the context. `AppContext.push()` calls `_app_var.set(self)` and keeps the returned token. `pop()` calls `_app_var.reset(token)` at `ctx.py:498`.\n- Because a `ContextVar` is isolated per thread and per asyncio task, each one sees its own context.\n- When nothing is pushed, the variable is unset. The proxy then raises a `RuntimeError` with the `unbound_message` text (\"Working outside of application/request context\").\n- `request` and `session` use the same `AppContext`. They only work when that context was created with a request, which `ctx.py:232` (`has_request`) checks.",
